# FI-2010 Equity Limit-Order-Book Signal Research

A leakage-resistant, point-in-time research system for three-way mid-price direction classification
on the official FI-2010 limit-order-book benchmark. The project is designed around the parts of
quantitative research that are easiest to get wrong: chronological validation, cumulative-fold
handling, model-selection leakage, confidence filtering, reproducibility, and irreversible final
holdout discipline.

> **Portfolio scope:** predictive LOB classification and confidence/coverage analysis. FI-2010 is
> normalised and anonymised, so this repository deliberately does **not** present simulated P&L,
> Sharpe, transaction-cost-adjusted returns, or live-trading profitability.

<!-- FI2010_RESULTS_START -->
## Results snapshot

- **Historical real development benchmark (v0.4; regenerated v0.6 evidence required)**
- **Anchored CF_1-CF_8 mean macro-F1:** 0.553
- **Worst development fold:** 0.509
- **Confidence-filtered development precision:** 78.1% at 8.0% coverage
- **CF_9:** sealed and unevaluated

![Historical anchored development stability](docs/results/fi2010/historical_development_macro_f1.png)

The historical figures above are retained only to show the already-observed development behaviour.
Version 0.6 expands the development-only model ladder from a fixed microstructure rule through
from-scratch statistical classifiers to boosted trees. The GitHub results block is automatically
replaced by validated v0.6 evidence after the final one-shot release workflow.
<!-- FI2010_RESULTS_END -->

## What this project demonstrates

- **Market microstructure:** 144-dimensional limit-order-book snapshots and publisher-defined
  short-horizon mid-price direction labels.
- **Anchored walk-forward research:** each `Train_CF_n` is evaluated only against its matching
  `Test_CF_n`; cumulative training files are never concatenated.
- **Leakage-resistant model selection:** class weights, scaling, candidate choice and confidence
  threshold selection use development information only.
- **Interpretable-to-nonlinear model ladder:** naive baselines, a fixed liquidity-pressure rule,
  from-scratch NumPy diagonal LDA/ridge/softmax models, sklearn SGD, audited histogram boosting and
  a compact LightGBM grid all compete on the same CF_1-CF_8 protocol.
- **Confidence-aware signals:** the classifier can abstain instead of forcing a direction on every
  snapshot; the report exposes the precision/coverage frontier rather than a cherry-picked accuracy.
- **Strict final-holdout discipline:** the chosen model is frozen and refitted on `Train_CF_9`; the
  real `Test_CF_9` payload is behind a source-bound, durable, one-shot release gate.
- **Reproducibility:** source/config/runtime/implementation hashes, content-addressed artifacts,
  deterministic ranking, regression tests and a synthetic end-to-end rehearsal.
- **Portfolio-ready evidence:** the final report produces charts, machine-readable metrics and
  CV-ready bullets, then publishes only small validated evidence into `docs/results/fi2010/`.

## Registered FI-2010 study

| Item | Registration |
|---|---|
| Representation | `NoAuction/1.NoAuction_Zscore` |
| Features | Source rows 1-144 |
| Labels | Source rows 145-149 |
| Classes | `1=up`, `2=stationary`, `3=down` |
| Primary horizon | Label row 4: 5 sampled steps / conventionally 50 LOB events |
| Development | Paired CF_1-CF_8 anchored folds |
| Final refit | `Train_CF_9` only |
| Final holdout | One-shot `Test_CF_9` |
| Primary metric | Macro-F1 |
| Secondary metrics | Balanced accuracy, log loss, MCC, per-class precision/recall/F1 |
| Signal diagnostics | Directional precision, coverage and abstention |

The model selection rule is fixed: **highest mean macro-F1 over CF_1-CF_8**, then highest worst-fold
macro-F1, then lower registered complexity, then stable specification ID.

## Model search

Version 0.6 deliberately compares increasing levels of model complexity before LightGBM. This makes
the research question more interesting than a single library-model benchmark: **how much predictive
value comes from interpretable microstructure/statistical structure, and how much requires nonlinear
boosted trees?**

The registered ladder is:

1. always-stationary and class-prior baselines;
2. a fixed **manual liquidity-pressure rule** using the 10-level basic book features and accumulated
   volume-difference feature;
3. a **from-scratch NumPy diagonal LDA** with pooled variance shrinkage and equal class priors;
4. **from-scratch NumPy multiclass ridge regression** over three registered L2 values;
5. **from-scratch NumPy multinomial softmax regression** trained with class-balanced Adam;
6. two sklearn `SGDClassifier(loss="log_loss")` regularisation settings;
7. the audited sklearn `HistGradientBoostingClassifier` candidate;
8. nine LightGBM combinations: learning rate `{0.03, 0.05, 0.08}` x leaves `{15, 31, 63}` with a
   fixed 180-tree budget and fixed regularisation/subsampling settings.

The first four non-trivial families are implemented directly in NumPy or as a fixed transparent rule,
so their mechanics can be explained line by line in an interview. The manual rule is intentionally a
**standardised depth-pressure proxy**, not a raw queue-imbalance ratio, because the public study uses
the publisher's Z-score representation. The final holdout is never used to choose among models.

The previously audited HGB candidate stays in the registered universe even when LightGBM is installed,
so the expanded search cannot erase the historical benchmark simply by switching implementations.

## Research architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Official FI-2010 outer ZIP] --> B[SHA-256 + size verification]
    B --> C[Secure nested ZIP import]
    C --> D[Target-blind manifest audit]
    D --> E[CF_1-CF_8 paired development]
    E --> F[Candidate + confidence-rule selection]
    F --> G[Freeze source/config/code/runtime hashes]
    G --> H[Refit frozen model on Train_CF_9]
    H --> I{Exact release phrase?}
    I -->|No| J[CF_9 remains sealed]
    I -->|Yes, once| K[Durable claim + seal]
    K --> L[Test_CF_9 one-shot evaluation]
    L --> M[Completion anchor + final report]
    M --> N[GitHub portfolio evidence + CV summary]
```

More detail: [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md),
[docs/model_ladder.md](docs/model_ladder.md),
[reports/fi2010_methodology.md](reports/fi2010_methodology.md), and the
[results/discussion note](reports/results_and_discussion.md).

## Reproduce the study

The official source archive is expected at `Downloads\FI-2010-official.zip`. Raw/extracted data and
model binaries are gitignored. If the verified archive and `data\raw\fi2010` already exist, v0.6
reuses them; there is **no second dataset download**.

### 1. Build the complete pre-holdout release candidate

From the repository root, activate `.venv` and run one command:

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
.\scripts\prepare_fi2010_release.ps1 `
    -InstallDependencies `
    -ArtifactDirectory 'artifacts\fi2010-v060'
```

This installs/verifies the FI-2010 dependency set (including LightGBM and Ruff), verifies the exact
source archive, reuses/imports the verified inner ZIP, runs the dedicated regression suite and static
checks, performs the target-blind audit, evaluates the bounded model search on CF_1-CF_8, freezes the
winner, refits on Train_CF_9 and creates `report-development`. It does **not** open Test_CF_9.

Review `artifacts\fi2010-v060\report-development\fi2010_evidence.md`, then commit the exact
source/configuration state before releasing the holdout.

### 2. Run the final holdout exactly once

```powershell
.\scripts\run_fi2010_holdout_report.ps1 `
    -ArtifactDirectory 'artifacts\fi2010-v060' `
    -Acknowledgement 'RELEASE FI2010 CF9 HOLDOUT ONCE'
```

That single command evaluates CF_9, builds the final charts/report and publishes the validated small
portfolio artifacts into `docs/results/fi2010/`. Changing the output directory cannot create another
valid release. The retained CF_9 result is never tuned away after inspection.

See [docs/final_release_checklist.md](docs/final_release_checklist.md) for the integrity checklist.

## Generated evidence

A completed final run creates:

```text
artifacts/fi2010-v060/
├── development/development_results.json
├── freeze/frozen_candidate.json
├── freeze/final_model_manifest.json
├── holdout/holdout_result.json
└── report-final/
    ├── fi2010_evidence.md
    ├── fi2010_evidence.json
    ├── portfolio_metrics.json
    ├── cv_summary.md
    ├── development_macro_f1_by_fold.png
    ├── model_comparison.png
    ├── confidence_precision_coverage.png
    └── development_vs_holdout.png
```

The GitHub-facing publisher copies only validated small evidence and charts. It never publishes raw
FI-2010 payloads or the fitted model binary.

## Tests and integrity checks

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m ruff check .
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m unittest tests.test_fi2010 -v
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m lob_alpha.cli fi2010-run-synthetic `
    --output-dir artifacts\fi2010-synthetic-check
git diff --check
```

The synthetic run exercises import → audit → development → selection → freeze/refit → one-shot
holdout → report without creating real empirical claims.

